- name: appsflyer
  type: table
  desc: >-
    Functions and constants for [AppsFlyer](https://www.appsflyer.com/) install attribution, consent
    signals, customer IDs and in-app events on Android and iOS. The module is available only on these
    platforms. Configure appsflyer.key in game.project and, on iOS, the numeric appsflyer.apple_app_id
    without the id prefix. The SDK initializes during app startup; Lua controls when session delivery
    starts.
  members:
    - name: start_sdk
      type: function
      desc: >-
        Enables session delivery once SDK 7 reports readiness. Call after registering a callback and setting
        the customer ID, consent and other pre-start options. Later foreground sessions start automatically.
        Repeated calls do not duplicate a session in the same foreground cycle. Raises a Lua error if
        required configuration is missing. After stop_sdk(true), call stop_sdk(false) before start_sdk();
        starting alone does not clear the stopped flag. Resumption waits for native readiness. See the
        [Android](https://dev.appsflyer.com/hc/docs/migrate-android-sdk-to-v7) and
        [iOS](https://dev.appsflyer.com/hc/docs/migrate-ios-sdk-to-v7) migration guides.
      examples:
        - desc: |-
            ```lua
            function init(self)
                if not appsflyer then return end
                appsflyer.set_callback(function(self, message_id, message)
                    if message_id == appsflyer.START_SUCCESS then
                        print("Session delivered")
                    elseif message.error then
                        print(message.code, message.error)
                    end
                end)
                appsflyer.set_customer_user_id("your_customer_id")
                -- Apply the user's consent choices before starting.
                appsflyer.start_sdk()
            end
            ```
    - name: set_callback
      type: function
      desc: >-
        Registers the single SDK callback, replacing the previous one. Pass nil to remove it, including in
        the script's final function. It is safe to replace or remove the callback from inside a callback.
        Native responses are queued and delivered during Defold's update on the Lua thread. Register before
        start_sdk.
      parameters:
        - name: callback
          type: function
          desc: >-
            Callback function, or nil to remove it.
          parameters:
            - name: self
              type: object
              desc: >-
                The script instance that registered the callback.
            - name: message_id
              type: number
              desc: >-
                One of appsflyer.CONVERSION_DATA_SUCCESS, appsflyer.CONVERSION_DATA_FAIL, appsflyer.START_SUCCESS,
                appsflyer.START_FAIL, appsflyer.EVENT_SUCCESS or appsflyer.EVENT_FAIL. Use named constants instead
                of numeric literals.
            - name: message
              type: table
              desc: >-
                An empty table for START_SUCCESS, the native attribution dictionary for CONVERSION_DATA_SUCCESS, or
                the fields below for event/error messages. Conversion data arrives independently of request
                acknowledgments.
              fields:
                - name: event_name
                  type: string
                  optional: true
                  desc: >-
                    Event name for EVENT_SUCCESS and EVENT_FAIL. Same-name events have no separate request ID.
                - name: error
                  type: string
                  optional: true
                  desc: >-
                    Native error description for START_FAIL, EVENT_FAIL and CONVERSION_DATA_FAIL.
                - name: code
                  type: number
                  optional: true
                  desc: >-
                    Native error code on failure. Codes differ by platform; Android conversion failures use 0.
                - name: af_status
                  type: string
                  optional: true
                  desc: >-
                    Attribution status when supplied by CONVERSION_DATA_SUCCESS, such as Organic or Non-organic.
                - name: is_first_launch
                  type: boolean
                  optional: true
                  desc: >-
                    First-launch flag when supplied by CONVERSION_DATA_SUCCESS. Other native fields are preserved.
      examples:
        - desc: |-
            ```lua
            local function on_appsflyer(self, message_id, message)
                if message_id == appsflyer.EVENT_SUCCESS then
                    print("Event delivered:", message.event_name)
                elseif message_id == appsflyer.CONVERSION_DATA_SUCCESS then
                    pprint(message)
                elseif message.error then
                    print("AppsFlyer error:", message.code, message.error)
                end
            end

            function init(self)
                if appsflyer then appsflyer.set_callback(on_appsflyer) end
            end

            function final(self)
                if appsflyer then appsflyer.set_callback(nil) end
            end
            ```
    - name: set_customer_user_id
      type: function
      desc: >-
        Sets your customer identifier on Android and iOS. Set it on every cold start before start_sdk to
        associate it with the first session. SDK 7 does not persist the value across process restarts. This
        is separate from the AppsFlyer installation ID returned by get_appsflyer_uid. Updates apply to
        future requests. Original docs:
        [Android](https://dev.appsflyer.com/hc/docs/android-sdk-reference-appsflyerlib#setcustomeruserid),
        [iOS](https://dev.appsflyer.com/hc/docs/ios-sdk-reference-appsflyerlib#customeruserid).
      parameters:
        - name: user_id
          type: string
          desc: >-
            Your application's customer identifier.
      examples:
        - desc: |-
            ```lua
            appsflyer.set_customer_user_id("your_customer_id")
            appsflyer.start_sdk()
            ```
    - name: get_appsflyer_uid
      type: function
      desc: >-
        Returns the native AppsFlyer installation identifier, or nil if unavailable. It is not your customer
        ID. Read after initialization, for example in START_SUCCESS. Original docs:
        [Android](https://dev.appsflyer.com/hc/docs/android-sdk-reference-appsflyerlib#getappsflyeruid),
        [iOS](https://dev.appsflyer.com/hc/docs/ios-sdk-reference-appsflyerlib#getappsflyeruid).
      return:
        - name: uid
          type: string
          desc: >-
            AppsFlyer installation ID, or nil if unavailable.
    - name: get_sdk_version
      type: function
      desc: >-
        Returns the loaded native SDK version, including any build information. Available even when
        credentials are missing. Use it when reporting integration issues. Original docs:
        [Android](https://dev.appsflyer.com/hc/docs/android-sdk-reference-appsflyerlib#getsdkversion),
        [iOS](https://dev.appsflyer.com/hc/docs/ios-sdk-reference-appsflyerlib#getsdkversion).
      return:
        - name: version
          type: string
          desc: >-
            Native SDK version string; it may contain a prefix or build suffix.
      examples:
        - desc: |-
            ```lua
            print(appsflyer.get_sdk_version())
            ```
    - name: set_debug_log
      type: function
      desc: >-
        Enables or disables native SDK diagnostics. Can be set before start_sdk; appsflyer.is_debug in
        game.project also controls startup logging. Disable for release builds. Native logs may contain the
        Dev Key and identifiers. Original docs:
        [Android](https://dev.appsflyer.com/hc/docs/android-sdk-reference-appsflyerlib#setdebuglog),
        [iOS](https://dev.appsflyer.com/hc/docs/ios-sdk-reference-appsflyerlib#isdebug).
      parameters:
        - name: is_debug
          type: boolean
          desc: >-
            True to enable debug logging, false to disable it.
    - name: log_event
      type: function
      desc: >-
        Logs an in-app event after start_sdk. EVENT_SUCCESS or EVENT_FAIL reports the native request result.
        Missing initialization raises a Lua error. Parameters must be a flat table with string keys and
        string/number values; numbers retain this extension's existing string serialization. Nested tables
        and booleans are rejected. An af_purchase event records revenue but does not validate a purchase
        receipt. Original docs:
        [Android](https://dev.appsflyer.com/hc/docs/android-sdk-reference-appsflyerlib#logevent),
        [iOS](https://dev.appsflyer.com/hc/docs/ios-sdk-reference-appsflyerlib#logevent).
      parameters:
        - name: event_name
          type: string
          desc: >-
            Event name, such as af_level_achieved, af_purchase or an application-defined name.
        - name: event_params
          type: table
          optional: true
          desc: >-
            String-keyed table of string/number values; may be omitted or nil for an empty event.
      examples:
        - desc: |-
            ```lua
            appsflyer.log_event("af_level_achieved", { af_level = 2, af_score = 100 })
            appsflyer.log_event("af_purchase", {
                af_currency = "USD",
                af_content_id = "item_id",
                af_revenue = 1.99,
            })
            ```
    - name: set_consent_data
      type: function
      desc: >-
        Supplies the user's explicit consent signals to the native SDK. Set the current choices on every
        cold start before start_sdk, and update them when they change. All four fields are optional
        booleans: omitted/nil means unspecified, whereas false is an explicit negative choice. Unknown
        fields and non-boolean values raise Lua errors. This function neither displays a consent dialog nor
        stops SDK delivery. Original docs:
        [Android](https://dev.appsflyer.com/hc/docs/android-sdk-reference-appsflyerlib#setconsentdata),
        [iOS](https://dev.appsflyer.com/hc/docs/ios-sdk-reference-appsflyerlib#setconsentdata).
      parameters:
        - name: consent
          type: table
          desc: >-
            Consent choices. An empty table forwards all four signals as unspecified.
          fields:
            - name: is_user_subject_to_gdpr
              type: boolean
              optional: true
              desc: >-
                Whether the user is subject to GDPR.
            - name: has_consent_for_data_usage
              type: boolean
              optional: true
              desc: >-
                Whether the user consented to data usage.
            - name: has_consent_for_ads_personalization
              type: boolean
              optional: true
              desc: >-
                Whether the user consented to personalized advertising.
            - name: has_consent_for_ad_storage
              type: boolean
              optional: true
              desc: >-
                Whether the user consented to advertising storage/access on the device.
      examples:
        - desc: |-
            ```lua
            -- Populate choices from your consent flow.
            local function apply_consent(choices)
                appsflyer.set_consent_data({
                    is_user_subject_to_gdpr = choices.gdpr,
                    has_consent_for_data_usage = choices.data_usage,
                    has_consent_for_ads_personalization = choices.personalized_ads,
                    has_consent_for_ad_storage = choices.ad_storage,
                })
                appsflyer.start_sdk()
            end
            ```
    - name: enable_tcf_data_collection
      type: function
      desc: >-
        Enables collection of TCF data stored by a compatible consent management platform. Configure before
        start_sdk on each cold start. Does not show a consent dialog or create a TCF string. Explicit
        signals supplied through set_consent_data take precedence. Original docs:
        [Android](https://dev.appsflyer.com/hc/docs/android-sdk-reference-appsflyerlib#enabletcfdatacollection),
         [iOS](https://dev.appsflyer.com/hc/docs/ios-sdk-reference-appsflyerlib#enabletcfdatacollection).
      parameters:
        - name: enabled
          type: boolean
          desc: >-
            True to enable TCF collection, false to disable it.
      examples:
        - desc: |-
            ```lua
            -- After your CMP has stored the user's TCF choices:
            appsflyer.enable_tcf_data_collection(true)
            appsflyer.start_sdk()
            ```
    - name: anonymize_user
      type: function
      desc: >-
        Enables or disables AppsFlyer's anonymization mode. Apply before start_sdk to affect the first
        session. Requests continue; use stop_sdk(true) to stop delivery. Changing this flag does not rewrite
        previously delivered data. Reapply your intended configuration on each cold start. Original docs:
        [Android](https://dev.appsflyer.com/hc/docs/android-sdk-reference-appsflyerlib#anonymizeuser),
        [iOS](https://dev.appsflyer.com/hc/docs/ios-sdk-reference-appsflyerlib#anonymizeuser).
      parameters:
        - name: enabled
          type: boolean
          desc: >-
            True to enable SDK anonymization, false to disable it.
    - name: stop_sdk
      type: function
      desc: >-
        Sets the native SDK stopped flag. Passing true also revokes the extension's automatic
        foreground-session gate. To resume, call stop_sdk(false), then start_sdk(); a session is sent when
        native session readiness permits it. Passing false alone does not re-enable a gate revoked by
        stop_sdk(true). Calls are queued on the platform UI/main thread; is_stopped may briefly return the
        previous value until the call has been applied. Already delivered data is unaffected. Original docs:
        [Android](https://dev.appsflyer.com/hc/docs/android-sdk-reference-appsflyerlib#stop),
        [iOS](https://dev.appsflyer.com/hc/docs/ios-sdk-reference-appsflyerlib#isstopped).
      parameters:
        - name: stopped
          type: boolean
          desc: >-
            True to stop SDK delivery, false to clear the native stopped flag.
      examples:
        - desc: |-
            ```lua
            appsflyer.stop_sdk(true)
            -- Later, when the application intends to resume:
            appsflyer.stop_sdk(false)
            appsflyer.start_sdk()
            ```
    - name: is_stopped
      type: function
      desc: >-
        Reads the native SDK stopped flag. This does not indicate whether start_sdk was called, whether the
        SDK is session-ready, or whether a request succeeded. A queued stop_sdk call can take effect after
        this getter returns. Original docs:
        [Android](https://dev.appsflyer.com/hc/docs/android-sdk-reference-appsflyerlib#isstopped),
        [iOS](https://dev.appsflyer.com/hc/docs/ios-sdk-reference-appsflyerlib#isstopped).
      return:
        - name: stopped
          type: boolean
          desc: >-
            True if the native SDK is stopped, false otherwise.
    - name: set_currency_code
      type: function
      desc: >-
        Sets the default revenue currency. Use a three-letter uppercase ISO 4217 code; other formats raise a
        Lua error. Apply before start_sdk and reapply on each cold start. An event's af_currency parameter
        can specify its own currency. Original docs:
        [Android](https://dev.appsflyer.com/hc/docs/android-sdk-reference-appsflyerlib#setcurrencycode),
        [iOS](https://dev.appsflyer.com/hc/docs/ios-sdk-reference-appsflyerlib#currencycode).
      parameters:
        - name: currency
          type: string
          desc: >-
            Currency code, for example USD, EUR or SEK. Format is checked; membership in ISO 4217 is not.
      examples:
        - desc: |-
            ```lua
            appsflyer.set_currency_code("EUR")
            ```
    - name: set_sharing_filter_for_partners
      type: function
      desc: >-
        Excludes partners from data sharing. Apply before start_sdk to affect the first session and reapply
        on each cold start. Use exact AppsFlyer partner IDs, not display names. Each ID must contain 1-45
        ASCII letters, digits or underscores. The special ID "all" excludes every partner. An empty table
        resets the filter. AppsFlyer continues receiving events. Malformed or sparse arrays raise a Lua
        error. Original docs:
        [Android](https://dev.appsflyer.com/hc/docs/android-sdk-reference-appsflyerlib#setsharingfilterforpartners),
        [iOS](https://dev.appsflyer.com/hc/docs/ios-sdk-reference-appsflyerlib#setsharingfilterforpartners).
      parameters:
        - name: partners
          type: table
          desc: >-
            Contiguous array of partner ID strings, starting at index 1, or an empty table to reset.
      examples:
        - desc: |-
            ```lua
            appsflyer.set_sharing_filter_for_partners({ "examplePartner1_int" })
            appsflyer.set_sharing_filter_for_partners({ "all" })
            appsflyer.set_sharing_filter_for_partners({}) -- Reset.
            ```
    - name: CONVERSION_DATA_SUCCESS
      type: number
      desc: >-
        Conversion data received. The message is the native attribution table; fields depend on the
        attribution result.
    - name: CONVERSION_DATA_FAIL
      type: number
      desc: >-
        Conversion request failed. The message contains error and code; Android conversion errors use code
        0.
    - name: START_SUCCESS
      type: number
      desc: >-
        Native SDK reports successful session delivery. The message is an empty table.
    - name: START_FAIL
      type: number
      desc: >-
        Native SDK reports failed session delivery. The message contains error and code.
    - name: EVENT_SUCCESS
      type: number
      desc: >-
        Native SDK reports successful event delivery. The message contains event_name.
    - name: EVENT_FAIL
      type: number
      desc: >-
        Native SDK reports failed event delivery. The message contains event_name, error and code.
